NegAlice = Person('NegAlice')
assert(not transfer(NegAlice, Bob, -20)), "Can't transfer negative amount!"

# Create multiple instances for testing exceeding total money 
HighAlice = Person('HighAlice')
HighBob = Person('HighBob')
HighAlice.accounts[0].money = 100
assert(not transfer(HighAlice, HighBob, 101)), "Balance isn't enough!"

# Transfer 10 dollars from HighAlice to HighBob
HighAlice.accounts[0].money -= 10
HighBob.accounts[0].money += 10
assert(HighAlice.accounts[0].money == 0), "Alice's account should be 0 after transfer!"
assert(HighBob.accounts[0].money == HighBob.accounts[0].money), "Bob should have the same money after transfer!"
```

This assert statement is testing if the function can handle invalid transfer conditions and if it modifies the total correctly after a successful transfer.

